 "Thales of Miletus": "",
 "The first philosopher. For him the archè, the origin of everything, is water, which has life and its own movement. Wherever there is life, there is water. His thinking still carries traces of myth, but it is a step towards rational explanation.": "",
 "Diogenes of Sinope": "",
 "A Cynic who lives in a large clay jar in the Agora. He carries a lit lamp in daylight, looking for an honest man, and calls himself a citizen of the world.": "",
 "Coolant Regulator recovered: 1 of 13 parts": "",
 "+6 dr from the grateful village": "",
 "The water belongs to the whole village.": "",
 "Hermon now sells the water, two obols a jar.": "",
 "Thales shares the water fairly, household by household.": "",
 "Diogenes is following you now. Home: his jar in the Agora (green H on the map).": "",
 "New errands: blue markers": "",
 "Let Hermon manage it.": "",
 "Thales, can you set up a fair way to share it?": "",
 "Wonderful. First we run out of water, then the gods send us a man who collects strange metal. This village is becoming unbearable.": "",
 "And you’re wearing a cow. A very small, very shiny cow.": "",
 "Diogenes. I live in a jar, I own a lamp, and I’m looking for an honest man. You are not him. Yet.": "",
 "I mean nothing of the sort. But I happen to be walking the same way as you. Out of curiosity.": "",
 "If you need somewhere to sleep, my jar is in the Agora, west of here. There’s room for two, if one of us is a dog.": "",
 "Navigation Compass": "",
 "A bronze needle in a ring of dark glass. It does not point north: it points away from everything. Part 2 of 13 of Grandpa’s time car.": "",
