 ", CH2.gnomonHarbour, ": "",
 "Bring the readings back to Anaximander": "",
 "Another season… The noon sun stands high in summer and low in winter. Two squares a short walk apart cannot have two seasons, unless they come from two different years.": "",
 "Two Miletuses, perhaps a century apart, sewn together like two pieces of leather. Mine, and one that comes after me.": "",
 "Prove it to me, stranger. Walk south down the road until you arrive. Mark a stone with chalk on the way, so you know it if you see it again.": "",
 "Walk Until You Arrive: mark the big stone by the road with chalk": "",
 "Find your chalk mark again": "",
 "Keep walking south down the road. Don’t stop.": "",
 "Mark the stone with chalk": "",
 ", npc: shepherd, text: ": "",
 "Like most roads to wisdom. And most conversations with philosophers.": "",
 "The Seam: follow the spinning compass west, to where the paving changes": "",
 "Look closely at the paving": "",
 "The seam": "",
 "Athenian marble and Milesian stone meet mid-step on the road between the Agora and the harbour. Moss has grown across the join: the fold is years old, not days.": "",
 "Then whoever sewed old Miletus to new Miletus did it long before you fell out of the sky. Interesting. Not that I care.": "",
 "Step through the seam": "",
 "I’ll wait here. I have a strict rule about places that don’t exist.": "",
 "Find the way out": "",
 "Apeiron: find the Navigation Compass. Things change size as you near them, so trust your ears. Follow the hum.": "",
 "Drawing the Impossible: take the compass to Anaximander": "",
 "A needle that points away from everything… Then I was right. The source of all things has no limits. No edges. The apeiron.": "",
 "He’ll be selling it in jars by tomorrow.": "",
 "Melissa, the clean pinax. We draw Kosmopolis as it truly is: old Miletus, the seam, new Miletus, and the road that bites its own tail.": "",
 "People should know the shape of the ground they stand on. Stranger, you walked the loop. You decide.": "",
 "Publish the map. People deserve the truth.": "",
 "Good. A true map frightens people for a week. A false one kills them for a century.": "",
 "Keep it secret, for now.": "",
 "Hmph. A secret map. My teacher would laugh. Very well. For now.": "",
 "Look: your needle trembles towards the hills. The villagers say the air up there has gone wrong. Thick by morning, thin as fire by noon.": "",
 "Wonderful. Bad air. I’ll bring my lamp.": "",
 "Anaximander of Miletus": "",
 "Student of Thales. For him the origin of everything is the apeiron, the boundless: something without limits or fixed qualities. Opposites like hot and cold separate out of it. He imagined the earth floating unsupported at the centre of everything, and is said to have drawn one of the first maps of the world and introduced the gnomon to Greece.": "",
 "Navigation Compass recovered: ": "",
 " of 13 parts": "",
 "The map is out. People trust your warnings, but the market empties for a while.": "",
 "The fold stays secret. Melissa trusts you.": "",
 "Clue: the seam is old. Moss grows across it. The fold is years old, not days.": "",
 "Next: the hills, where the air has gone wrong.": "",
 "Turbo Lung": "",
 "A bronze-and-leather bellows that breathes by itself. Its valve is stamped with tiny letters: L.M. Workshop. Part 3 of 13.": "",
