 "It’s easier to breathe now. It smells like wet wool.": "",
 "*cough* The air hurts in the mornings. *cough*": "",
 "The breathing cave": "",
 "Hide in a side niche when the cave breathes out!": "",
 "Leave the cave": "",
 "Anaximenes of Miletus. A village where the air has gone wrong.": "",
 "Climb the road to the hill village and find Anaximenes": "",
 "Breathe! Breathe, all of you! Do you feel it? This morning the air was thick as wool. By noon it will be thin as fire!": "",
 ", npc: eudora, text: ": "",
 "Forgive me, Eudora. But everything is air: thickened, it becomes wind, then cloud, then water, then earth and stone. Thinned out, it becomes fire.": "",
 "Making it? Hm. I had assumed the gods were finally reading my work. But you are right to ask. Go and feel the air for yourself.": "",
 "At the well, on the threshing floor, and up on the ridge. Tell me where it is thickest.": "",
 "I’ll stay here and breathe professionally.": "",
 "Feel the air": "",
 "Felt and Stone: tell Anaximenes what you found": "",
 "A breathing cave! Wonderful. But first, a small experiment, so you understand what you are hunting. Breathe on your hand.": "",
 "Once with your mouth wide open. Once with your lips pressed tight. Which breath is warm?": "",
 "Mouth open: the breath is warm.": "",
 "Yes! Loose air spreads out and is warm. Squeezed air, pressed thick through tight lips, is cold.": "",
 "Lips pressed: the breath is warm.": "",
 "Ha! Your hand knows better than your tongue. Loose air is warm. Squeezed air is cold.": "",
 "Thick is cold, thin is hot. One stuff, many forms. Whatever is in that cave is squeezing and loosening the very air we live in.": "",
 "But Eudora will not let you near her hill until her boy can breathe. Help her first. She trusts hands, not theories.": "",
 "The Healer’s Problem: take a clean cloth from Eudora’s loom": "",
 "Fill a pot of water at the well": "",
