 "Two days of slow, gentle air. Look at him, stranger. Look at my son.": "",
 ", npc: kimon, text: off ? ": "",
 "I ran to the well and back! Twice! Without coughing!": "",
 "One stuff, made thick and made thin, and a village sick or healthy depending on which. You see? Air is everything.": "",
 "Air is free. That’s the only thing I like about it.": "",
 "“Ask the man who hears numbers.” That can only mean one person. Pythagoras. And his brotherhood does not like strangers.": "",
 "Anaximenes of Miletus": "",
 "The third thinker of Miletus. For him the origin of everything is air. Condensed, it becomes wind, cloud, water, earth and stone; rarefied, it becomes fire. One process, condensation and rarefaction, explains how a single substance becomes many.": "",
 "Turbo Lung recovered: ": "",
 "Kimon had a hard night, but your steam tent pulled him through.": "",
 "You waited two days. The village healed before you took the Lung.": "",
 "Clue: the valve says “L.M. Workshop”. Grandpa’s shop.": "",
 "Athens is open: Captain Nausikles sails from the middle pier of the harbour.": "",
 "Next: Pythagoras and the brotherhood, on Samos. Captain Nausikles can take you.": "",
